constructed
route: GET /tasks/<pod>/<id>
status: 200
built-from: task-failed-base-ref-folder.json (the constructed one this capture replaced, itself task-failed-pipeline.json with a folder's sentence) with the reason and failureKind of a task whose approval nobody answered by its expiresAt
source: docket's report of its commit 4bf26e50 and of the 2026-10-31 run where Tack resolved an approval with deny after its own timeout: docket now fails an approval nobody answered by its own expiresAt with failureKind approval_expired and reason "approval expired: nobody answered by <expiresAt>"; a sent deny stays approval_denied
docket: docket 0.2.0b6 (API 6), 4bf26e50 as reported, not read here and not run
date: 2026-10-31
note: stays constructed on purpose. The capture script spends no model and waits for nothing, and docket's own deadline for an approval is hours (the escalation of an enqueue a policy holds expires on its own clock), so no run of the script can reach an approval that expires. A live run that waits it out replaces this file. failureKind is an open string, docket may add values.
edited: 2026-11-04, `costUsd` removed (docket 0.3.0b1 at 1d180651 keeps no dollars)
